      "entity_type": "solution",
      "path": ".cg-docs/solutions/testing-patterns/2026-10-15-installed-r-checks-for-durable-request-convergence.md",
      "slug": "2026-10-15-installed-r-checks-for-durable-request-convergence",
      "status": "",
      "summary": "The stamp generic-request work needed to prove more than successful saving: after A changes from A1 to A2, B must execute against A2, yet may retain B1 when its result and producing proof are unchanged. C should then skip against B1. The old B1 snapshot must still name A1, while a new execution receipt names A2. The next identical request must perform no work, including after a fresh R process starts. Reviews found failures that an ordinary green save/load test did not cover: unintended replacement of explicit historical pins, unverified same-size parent byte edits, representation-dependent request IDs, abandoned receipt publication,...",
